WEBVTT

1
00:01:00,291 --> 00:01:04,500
AS OF THIS WEEK,
NINE WORKERS HAVE REPORTEDLY DIED.

2
00:01:06,958 --> 00:01:08,666
THE FIRST DEATH TOOK PLACE
ON FEBRUARY 12, 2025

3
00:01:09,708 --> 00:01:11,208
...ON THE EDGE OF NEHEA FOREST...

4
00:01:11,291 --> 00:01:12,791
...BY THE MINISTRY OF ENVIRONMENT...

5
00:01:15,291 --> 00:01:16,291
How's it going?

6
00:01:16,375 --> 00:01:17,333
You gonna be long?

7
00:01:18,500 --> 00:01:20,625
Just two more sentences.
Then I'll send it to Mr. Endy, sir.

8
00:01:20,708 --> 00:01:23,083
I told the printer guy to wait.

9
00:01:23,166 --> 00:01:27,416
But his wife started having the baby.
He had to rush to the hospital.

10
00:01:27,500 --> 00:01:29,000
THE NATIVES REPORTED THE CASE
TO THE HUMAN RIGHTS COMMISSION

11
00:01:29,083 --> 00:01:32,583
If we had ads, I could fill the space.
But we haven't had ads in a long time.

12
00:01:32,666 --> 00:01:33,875
"THIS FOREST ISN'T JUST TREES,
IT'S OUR HOME."

13
00:01:33,958 --> 00:01:36,958
If your article doesn't come in,
we'll have a blank spot.

14
00:01:41,833 --> 00:01:42,958
Done.

15
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:46,375
I just need to wait
for Mr. Endy's approval.

16
00:01:47,666 --> 00:01:49,958
I made sure that
there won't be any revisions.

17
00:01:50,041 --> 00:01:51,083
It should go straight to print.

18
00:01:51,166 --> 00:01:53,166
Of course you had to be careful.

19
00:01:53,250 --> 00:01:55,583
You're writing about a big company.

20
00:01:55,666 --> 00:01:57,708
Their investors are government officials.

21
00:01:57,791 --> 00:01:59,333
This will make headlines.

22
00:01:59,416 --> 00:02:02,541
They illegally dug up 10,000 hectares
of protected forest for a nickel mine.

23
00:02:03,125 --> 00:02:04,500
No one dares to speak up.

24
00:02:04,583 --> 00:02:06,875
Plus, dozens of workers died
under suspicious circumstances.

25
00:02:07,541 --> 00:02:08,416
It's scary, sir.

26
00:02:09,041 --> 00:02:10,500
And you actually went there?

27
00:02:10,583 --> 00:02:11,500
Yes, sir.

28
00:02:11,583 --> 00:02:15,250
It's a seven-hour drive
from Balikpapan to Nehea Forest.

29
00:02:15,666 --> 00:02:19,291
I've been to Borneo forests before,
but this one was really mysterious.

30
00:02:20,750 --> 00:02:23,625
I can't wait to read your piece.

31
00:02:23,708 --> 00:02:25,208
Best piece I've ever written.

32
00:02:25,291 --> 00:02:26,583
Mr. Endy's going to love it!

33
00:02:27,125 --> 00:02:28,125
That's great!

34
00:02:31,125 --> 00:02:32,125
Hello, sir?

35
00:02:32,208 --> 00:02:34,791
<i>You call this an article?
What are you, an intern?</i>

36
00:02:34,875 --> 00:02:36,125
<i>Get in here, now!</i>

37
00:02:36,208 --> 00:02:37,000
Yes, sir.

38
00:02:38,333 --> 00:02:39,416
Oh no.

39
00:02:41,041 --> 00:02:42,291
I'll be smoking downstairs, Dimas!

40
00:02:42,375 --> 00:02:43,666
Let me know once it's sent to me!

41
00:02:49,291 --> 00:02:50,416
Excuse me, sir.

42
00:02:50,500 --> 00:02:54,250
You went all the way to Borneo,
wasting our money for this?

43
00:02:55,041 --> 00:02:57,875
Writing about homicide
like those trashy online articles?

44
00:02:57,958 --> 00:02:59,958
You're an economics desk reporter!

45
00:03:00,750 --> 00:03:03,000
The illegal mining part is there, sir.

46
00:03:03,666 --> 00:03:05,708
But the workers' deaths are
more compelling...

47
00:03:05,791 --> 00:03:07,458
Don't you get that we're going
out of business?!

48
00:03:07,541 --> 00:03:11,250
People still read us
because we have substance!

49
00:03:12,875 --> 00:03:14,875
If our stories are no different
from anyone else's,

50
00:03:14,958 --> 00:03:16,833
why the hell would they subscribe to us?

51
00:03:17,458 --> 00:03:19,583
You've got 20 minutes to revise.

52
00:03:19,666 --> 00:03:24,750
The lede should be, "Illegal Deforestation
of Protected Forest."

53
00:03:24,833 --> 00:03:27,375
"Vice-President's son's company
is involved."

54
00:03:27,458 --> 00:03:28,250
That's it!

55
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:29,916
Yes, sir.

56
00:03:31,541 --> 00:03:32,416
Idiot!

57
00:03:33,666 --> 00:03:34,875
MY WIFE

58
00:03:36,916 --> 00:03:37,750
Hello?

59
00:03:38,583 --> 00:03:42,208
<i>You know the editor can handle it.
It doesn't have to be you.</i>

60
00:03:43,208 --> 00:03:45,500
I just fired my editor today.

61
00:03:45,583 --> 00:03:46,791
I can't afford to pay them!

62
00:03:47,500 --> 00:03:50,458
<i>If the company can't be saved,
then come home.</i>

63
00:03:50,958 --> 00:03:52,916
<i>Save your marriage!</i>

64
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:57,000
I built this paper from nothing!
Before I met you!

65
00:03:57,083 --> 00:03:59,708
This paper means a lot more
than our marriage!

66
00:04:00,958 --> 00:04:02,375
<i>Fine. Bye.</i>

67
00:04:04,291 --> 00:04:05,625
Fuck!

68
00:05:08,333 --> 00:05:09,125
Dimas!

69
00:05:10,583 --> 00:05:11,541
Mr. Vijay...

70
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:12,791
Help...

71
00:05:34,583 --> 00:05:36,500
MAINTAIN ORDER

72
00:05:43,333 --> 00:05:44,916
Good morning!

73
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:47,666
Morning, morning, morning!

74
00:05:48,375 --> 00:05:50,750
Today is the same as yesterday,

75
00:05:50,833 --> 00:05:53,000
{\an8}the same as tomorrow.

76
00:05:53,791 --> 00:05:54,833
As always,

77
00:05:55,375 --> 00:05:59,875
you decide whether your day goes smoothly

78
00:06:00,458 --> 00:06:01,916
or the other way round.

79
00:06:02,375 --> 00:06:04,375
You know the rules.

80
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:08,250
Obey, and you live in peace.

81
00:06:08,333 --> 00:06:11,833
Disobey, and face the consequences.

82
00:06:11,916 --> 00:06:14,833
The only freedom you have here

83
00:06:15,875 --> 00:06:19,541
is choosing how you want
to spend your day.

84
00:06:20,916 --> 00:06:22,000
Understood?

85
00:06:22,083 --> 00:06:24,208
Understood, understood, understood!

86
00:06:24,625 --> 00:06:25,875
- Everyone's here?
- Yes, sir!

87
00:06:25,958 --> 00:06:27,625
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

88
00:06:27,708 --> 00:06:28,625
One missing!

89
00:06:41,041 --> 00:06:42,375
Get down.

90
00:06:42,458 --> 00:06:43,583
I'm sick, sir.

91
00:06:43,666 --> 00:06:45,708
If I stand, my head spins.

92
00:06:55,791 --> 00:06:57,458
Stand up!

93
00:07:22,791 --> 00:07:23,916
Idiot.

94
00:07:31,125 --> 00:07:32,625
He has no religion!

95
00:07:41,791 --> 00:07:43,000
What did you say?

96
00:07:45,750 --> 00:07:48,833
The next hour and a half is
for religious practice.

97
00:07:48,916 --> 00:07:50,291
He has no religion,

98
00:07:50,375 --> 00:07:52,583
so he can rest and recover.

99
00:07:52,666 --> 00:07:56,166
A third of your time here's for religion.

100
00:07:56,250 --> 00:08:01,750
So if you're not religious,
you get a third of the day off?

101
00:08:01,833 --> 00:08:05,291
Religion doesn't force
sick people to pray.

102
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:12,166
If you think you're smarter than me,

103
00:08:12,833 --> 00:08:14,750
don't fool yourself.

104
00:08:16,291 --> 00:08:20,708
Your brain's tiny compared to mine.

105
00:08:25,625 --> 00:08:27,208
Why so quiet?

106
00:08:29,458 --> 00:08:31,666
Picturing yourself as me?

107
00:08:33,333 --> 00:08:35,416
What would you be doing right now
if you were me?

108
00:08:36,458 --> 00:08:39,333
I definitely wouldn't work in
a shitty place like this.

109
00:08:42,625 --> 00:08:44,750
I work here

110
00:08:45,916 --> 00:08:47,750
because I can!

111
00:08:52,250 --> 00:08:53,208
Come on.

112
00:09:07,083 --> 00:09:08,125
Let him go!

113
00:09:09,208 --> 00:09:09,916
Come on!

114
00:09:10,500 --> 00:09:11,333
Fight back!

115
00:09:17,666 --> 00:09:18,500
Come on now.

116
00:09:19,208 --> 00:09:20,166
Come on!

117
00:09:27,791 --> 00:09:30,208
In here, you're excrement.

118
00:09:33,166 --> 00:09:36,208
So if someone gives a damn, like I do,

119
00:09:37,583 --> 00:09:38,791
just be grateful.

120
00:09:39,958 --> 00:09:41,666
Don't act out.

121
00:09:47,625 --> 00:09:48,875
Believe me!

122
00:09:52,083 --> 00:09:53,416
I'm harsh on you

123
00:09:54,750 --> 00:09:56,833
because that's what you need.

124
00:09:59,541 --> 00:10:02,708
I'm the cure to your diseased hearts.

125
00:10:03,375 --> 00:10:06,791
You're all here
because of your own mistakes.

126
00:10:07,791 --> 00:10:11,083
You have no right to complain.

127
00:10:11,166 --> 00:10:13,958
No right to ask for anything!

128
00:10:14,583 --> 00:10:18,750
Just be quiet and follow the rules.

129
00:10:19,791 --> 00:10:21,291
Now go do your religious activities!

130
00:10:22,541 --> 00:10:24,583
Whether you have a religion or not!

131
00:10:28,708 --> 00:10:29,916
Take him to the cage.

132
00:10:43,875 --> 00:10:47,541
No need to throw it like that.
It won't hurt you to be nice.

133
00:10:48,250 --> 00:10:50,666
What if I spit on it first?

134
00:10:55,750 --> 00:10:58,916
Why did Anggoro pick a fight
with Jefry earlier?

135
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:00,916
Better than this fucker dying.

136
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:03,833
I didn't ask Anggoro to help.
He thinks everyone needs his help.

137
00:11:03,916 --> 00:11:06,708
Without him, most of us
wouldn't survive in here.

138
00:11:06,791 --> 00:11:10,541
- Not me. I'm doing just fine.
- Fine getting beaten up?

139
00:11:10,625 --> 00:11:11,958
Anggoro's not even a good fighter.

140
00:11:12,041 --> 00:11:13,541
But people respect him.

141
00:11:14,041 --> 00:11:15,708
It's his looks.

142
00:11:15,791 --> 00:11:18,208
If I were tall and handsome like him,
people would respect me too.

143
00:11:18,291 --> 00:11:22,083
Handsome guys get stepped on too.
Anggoro's got a real leader's spirit.

144
00:11:22,166 --> 00:11:23,458
That's what he gets respect for.

145
00:11:24,458 --> 00:11:25,291
You?

146
00:11:25,375 --> 00:11:29,416
You're still alive only because
others think you can actually see ghosts.

147
00:11:31,333 --> 00:11:32,750
You lied about that?!

148
00:11:34,333 --> 00:11:35,708
You trying to get me killed?

149
00:11:36,625 --> 00:11:39,458
Confess, Six.
You don't want to die a sinner.

150
00:11:39,541 --> 00:11:41,000
- Right.
- Six.

151
00:11:41,416 --> 00:11:44,000
You really don't have religion?
Where will you go when you die?

152
00:11:44,916 --> 00:11:47,666
Six did a mantra when I was sick,
and I got better.

153
00:11:47,750 --> 00:11:48,666
You lied about that too?

154
00:11:50,041 --> 00:11:50,916
But you got better, right?

155
00:11:51,000 --> 00:11:52,000
Fucker.

156
00:11:52,083 --> 00:11:55,333
You're a former professor,
and you buy that nonsense?

157
00:11:55,416 --> 00:11:57,375
You're just fresh meat for the dumb.

158
00:11:57,458 --> 00:11:59,541
But Six has a point, Pendi.

159
00:11:59,625 --> 00:12:02,208
You read books every day,
but you're still dumb like us.

160
00:12:02,291 --> 00:12:06,166
If only you could outsmart Jefry
and show that we have brains too.

161
00:12:06,250 --> 00:12:10,375
I'm sick of hearing him lecture us.

162
00:12:10,458 --> 00:12:11,416
Hey, man.

163
00:12:11,500 --> 00:12:12,750
Where's Anggoro?

164
00:12:12,833 --> 00:12:15,083
He's not here. Go away.

165
00:12:16,375 --> 00:12:20,250
- Please help me, man. I'm fucked.
- It's none of our business, go away!

166
00:12:21,500 --> 00:12:23,666
Without Anggoro's help, I'm dead for sure.

167
00:12:23,750 --> 00:12:26,166
He's in the cage. He can't help you!

168
00:12:26,250 --> 00:12:29,875
Anggoro's not here, Syafiq.
Go away.

169
00:12:40,708 --> 00:12:41,625
Fuckers!

170
00:12:42,083 --> 00:12:43,291
You idiots!

171
00:12:47,083 --> 00:12:48,458
Don't you mess with me!

172
00:12:48,958 --> 00:12:50,541
You think you own this place?!

173
00:12:50,625 --> 00:12:55,291
Nothing is free in this world! Fuck you!

174
00:12:56,375 --> 00:12:57,541
Listen to me!

175
00:12:57,625 --> 00:13:02,333
Throwing food away
while people out there starve to death!

176
00:13:02,416 --> 00:13:06,208
You brainless fuckers!

177
00:13:06,291 --> 00:13:08,583
Lick it! Fucking lick it clean!

178
00:13:30,250 --> 00:13:31,541
You've got visitors.

179
00:13:32,708 --> 00:13:33,791
Tell them to go home.

180
00:13:34,875 --> 00:13:36,083
What am I, your servant?

181
00:13:39,916 --> 00:13:41,125
Tell them yourself.

182
00:13:41,916 --> 00:13:43,208
I feel bad just looking at their faces.

183
00:14:18,791 --> 00:14:19,916
Where's your mother?

184
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:22,125
It's just me and Didi, Dad.

185
00:14:22,208 --> 00:14:24,083
What are you doing here?

186
00:14:24,625 --> 00:14:26,708
We haven't seen each other in two months.

187
00:14:27,625 --> 00:14:29,000
We missed you.

188
00:14:30,875 --> 00:14:32,375
Mom didn't want to come.

189
00:14:33,375 --> 00:14:38,208
Our neighbor dropped us off
on his way to work.

190
00:14:38,291 --> 00:14:42,416
Your mom must've been busy
working hard for you guys.

191
00:14:42,500 --> 00:14:43,458
No, Dad.

192
00:14:43,541 --> 00:14:44,541
She...

193
00:14:45,416 --> 00:14:48,000
We think she's going out
with Mr. Alexander.

194
00:14:48,833 --> 00:14:49,791
Alexander who?

195
00:14:49,875 --> 00:14:52,625
Her coworker at the bakery.

196
00:14:52,708 --> 00:14:55,541
He's been visiting
for the last three months.

197
00:14:55,625 --> 00:14:59,666
At first, Mom kicked him out.
But he kept coming.

198
00:15:00,458 --> 00:15:03,291
And I think she's starting to like him.

199
00:15:03,833 --> 00:15:06,333
We don't want Mom to marry him, Dad.

200
00:15:06,416 --> 00:15:08,291
We don't want a father like him.

201
00:15:08,375 --> 00:15:09,291
Why?

202
00:15:10,041 --> 00:15:11,250
Because...

203
00:15:11,333 --> 00:15:12,583
He...

204
00:15:19,041 --> 00:15:20,208
He's ugly, Dad.

205
00:15:21,458 --> 00:15:23,625
Even with a name like Alexander.

206
00:15:23,708 --> 00:15:26,375
See, I'm Bibin, and I look okay.

207
00:15:28,125 --> 00:15:32,708
Your mom can't remarry.
We're still married.

208
00:15:32,791 --> 00:15:37,750
Mom said you were supposed
to be out last year,

209
00:15:37,833 --> 00:15:42,083
but you kept getting into fights,
so you're still here.

210
00:15:42,958 --> 00:15:43,791
Dad.

211
00:15:43,875 --> 00:15:48,333
Please don't fight anymore, Dad.

212
00:15:48,416 --> 00:15:51,750
Didi here asks everyone he meets,

213
00:15:51,833 --> 00:15:55,250
"Which prison is your dad in?"

214
00:15:56,875 --> 00:15:59,500
He thinks all dads are in prison.

215
00:16:01,125 --> 00:16:04,833
We look at your photo
every night before bed.

216
00:16:05,375 --> 00:16:07,000
So we won't forget your face.

217
00:16:08,041 --> 00:16:09,000
Oh, almost forgot.

218
00:16:12,833 --> 00:16:13,916
What's this?

219
00:16:14,000 --> 00:16:16,583
So you won't forget our faces.

220
00:16:23,375 --> 00:16:24,875
What are you playing with here?

221
00:16:24,958 --> 00:16:26,750
That's clay.

222
00:16:27,333 --> 00:16:28,791
We can make all kinds of shapes.

223
00:16:28,875 --> 00:16:37,375
Teacher said that liking to make shapes
is a sign of intelligence.

224
00:16:37,458 --> 00:16:41,166
You imagine it in your mind first,
then create it with your hands.

225
00:16:41,250 --> 00:16:45,125
She also said that it teaches us
to live with purpose.

226
00:16:45,208 --> 00:16:46,250
She's right.

227
00:16:49,083 --> 00:16:50,708
Time to go home now.

228
00:16:51,458 --> 00:16:52,708
Okay, Dad.

229
00:16:52,791 --> 00:16:54,833
Please don't get into trouble
anymore, Dad.

230
00:16:54,916 --> 00:16:56,083
I'm sorry.

231
00:17:03,500 --> 00:17:05,166
I brought you a banana.

232
00:17:07,333 --> 00:17:10,208
Bye, Dad!

233
00:17:10,291 --> 00:17:11,708
Bye, my sons.

234
00:17:28,041 --> 00:17:32,291
NO SMOKING
WELCOME

235
00:17:44,416 --> 00:17:45,333
Poor man.

236
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:48,333
Just about to repent and then got killed.

237
00:17:49,250 --> 00:17:50,625
Have a smoke and calm down.

238
00:17:52,416 --> 00:17:53,625
Hey, this is expensive.

239
00:17:53,708 --> 00:17:54,541
It's haram.

240
00:17:56,291 --> 00:17:57,833
He's not allowed.

241
00:17:58,333 --> 00:18:00,750
Why are you all squatting here
like egg yolks?

242
00:18:06,875 --> 00:18:07,875
What?

243
00:18:08,875 --> 00:18:11,416
Someone was looking for you,
asking for protection.

244
00:18:11,500 --> 00:18:12,333
Who?

245
00:18:12,958 --> 00:18:13,916
Syafiq.

246
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:15,833
Oh, heard he wants to quit dealing.

247
00:18:16,750 --> 00:18:18,625
Promised his sick mother.

248
00:18:19,333 --> 00:18:20,375
Where's he?

249
00:18:21,750 --> 00:18:23,166
He got stabbed to death.

250
00:18:24,541 --> 00:18:25,666
Don't look.

251
00:18:26,375 --> 00:18:27,250
I feel guilty now.

252
00:18:27,333 --> 00:18:31,333
You helped me this morning
and ended up in solitary,

253
00:18:31,416 --> 00:18:32,958
and you couldn't help Syafiq.

254
00:18:33,041 --> 00:18:34,458
It's not your fault.

255
00:18:35,166 --> 00:18:36,666
Who visited you?

256
00:18:37,458 --> 00:18:38,916
My kids.

257
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:40,083
What did they say?

258
00:18:40,791 --> 00:18:44,791
To make sure I stay out of trouble
so I can get out in seven months.

259
00:18:44,875 --> 00:18:46,000
And what did you tell them?

260
00:18:46,541 --> 00:18:47,375
Nothing.

261
00:18:48,583 --> 00:18:50,458
What's your plan when you get out?

262
00:18:50,541 --> 00:18:51,500
Nothing.

263
00:18:51,583 --> 00:18:53,916
There's no point.

264
00:18:54,000 --> 00:18:58,458
