513
00:32:55,333 --> 00:32:56,125
There.

514
00:32:56,666 --> 00:32:57,791
Don't mess with me.

515
00:33:06,625 --> 00:33:10,375
I can't take this anymore.
I'm better off dead...

516
00:33:11,333 --> 00:33:13,083
Can't you die quietly?

517
00:33:13,166 --> 00:33:15,541
I can't sleep, damn it!

518
00:33:16,208 --> 00:33:18,625
If you don't have religion,
where will you go when you die?

519
00:33:18,708 --> 00:33:19,958
I'll send him to hell myself.

520
00:33:20,041 --> 00:33:20,916
Shut it.

521
00:33:22,125 --> 00:33:23,500
It hurts...

522
00:33:43,041 --> 00:33:44,833
You're not sick anymore?

523
00:33:44,916 --> 00:33:46,250
No, I feel great.

524
00:33:48,833 --> 00:33:52,375
- He turned into Jackie Chan?
- Dude's lost his mind.

525
00:33:53,208 --> 00:33:56,000
Man, I feel like an athlete.

526
00:34:02,000 --> 00:34:04,166
Did he take the wrong meds?

527
00:34:26,041 --> 00:34:27,833
- What a mess.
- A shower would be nice.

528
00:34:27,916 --> 00:34:30,750
- I'll ask for AC later.
- The fan isn't even working.

529
00:34:38,708 --> 00:34:41,458
Vin, come here.
What are you doing over there?

530
00:34:42,291 --> 00:34:44,375
- Vin.
- Oh, shit.

531
00:34:45,083 --> 00:34:46,208
Where's Six?

532
00:34:46,291 --> 00:34:49,541
He took a shower earlier
and is exercising now.

533
00:34:54,916 --> 00:34:56,500
The kid's still alive?

534
00:34:56,583 --> 00:34:59,250
Tokek was too drunk
to kill him last night.

535
00:34:59,333 --> 00:35:01,500
But today, it will happen for sure.

536
00:35:01,583 --> 00:35:04,708
- Let's pray for him.
- Right.

537
00:35:06,125 --> 00:35:07,000
I'm off first.

538
00:35:07,083 --> 00:35:08,208
Okay.

539
00:35:38,791 --> 00:35:40,750
Pick it up, sweetheart.

540
00:35:44,125 --> 00:35:45,208
Pick it up!

541
00:35:47,666 --> 00:35:49,791
Don't bend over.

542
00:36:16,416 --> 00:36:21,458
Your hands are useless, huh?
Let me just cut them off for you.

543
00:36:38,375 --> 00:36:40,625
So you got yourself a little guard dog.

544
00:37:03,916 --> 00:37:06,708
You've got other creatures
living with you.

545
00:37:06,791 --> 00:37:10,208
Rats, cockroaches, bedbugs.

546
00:37:11,500 --> 00:37:16,333
Make your cell nice and comfy for them.

547
00:37:17,125 --> 00:37:20,208
You're able to be here because
the country is funding it.

548
00:37:20,291 --> 00:37:22,000
Be grateful!

549
00:37:22,500 --> 00:37:26,750
Clean your space until it's spotless!

550
00:37:30,958 --> 00:37:34,791
SHIT

551
00:39:24,583 --> 00:39:26,083
Fuck you!

552
00:39:52,916 --> 00:39:54,583
Fucker!

553
00:39:55,625 --> 00:39:58,041
What do you know about being fucked?

554
00:39:58,875 --> 00:40:02,958
Life has fucked me over so many times!

555
00:40:06,541 --> 00:40:08,541
Wanna feel what I feel?

556
00:40:09,125 --> 00:40:11,166
Come at me!

557
00:40:30,291 --> 00:40:32,125
This fucker.

558
00:40:38,250 --> 00:40:39,541
Fucker!

559
00:42:01,375 --> 00:42:02,833
Fuck! What's with you!

560
00:42:03,208 --> 00:42:04,041
You two!

561
00:42:04,833 --> 00:42:07,250
Why is it always you two?

562
00:42:07,958 --> 00:42:10,083
You think this prison--

563
00:42:15,125 --> 00:42:17,000
What's going on?

564
00:42:44,875 --> 00:42:46,083
Who did it?

565
00:42:46,166 --> 00:42:47,541
We'll sort it out
before the police arrive, sir.

566
00:42:47,625 --> 00:42:49,708
They can't and won't come here.

567
00:42:49,791 --> 00:42:50,708
Are you stupid?

568
00:42:50,791 --> 00:42:53,041
If this hits the headlines, we're screwed.

569
00:42:53,125 --> 00:42:55,833
He was a nobody.
Even his family won't show.

570
00:42:55,916 --> 00:42:57,291
- Handle it yourself.
- Yes, sir.

571
00:42:57,375 --> 00:43:01,083
This isn't just about me.
If I go down, you're going down with me.

572
00:43:01,166 --> 00:43:04,000
- You're already in too deep. Swim smart.
- Understood, sir.

573
00:43:04,083 --> 00:43:04,833
Find out who--

574
00:43:04,916 --> 00:43:07,208
Everything okay, Mr. Sapto?

575
00:43:07,291 --> 00:43:09,666
Sir! So sorry if we disturbed your rest.

576
00:43:09,750 --> 00:43:10,458
All is good, sir.

577
00:43:10,541 --> 00:43:17,583
We've got all the officers
ensuring your comfort and safety.

578
00:43:19,000 --> 00:43:19,958
Thank goodness.

579
00:43:20,041 --> 00:43:21,458
Yes.

580
00:43:21,541 --> 00:43:24,375
I'm trying to be a model citizen now.

581
00:43:24,458 --> 00:43:25,291
Right.

582
00:43:25,375 --> 00:43:27,666
- Not going anywhere.
- I understand.

583
00:43:27,750 --> 00:43:31,125
Just staying in my cell. Safe, right?

584
00:43:31,208 --> 00:43:33,041
Of course, sir.

585
00:43:35,375 --> 00:43:39,875
I'll probably head home next week.

586
00:43:39,958 --> 00:43:42,541
I haven't been home in a week.
My poor wife must miss me.

587
00:43:42,625 --> 00:43:44,291
Wife number...?

588
00:43:44,375 --> 00:43:46,083
The third one, of course.

589
00:43:46,750 --> 00:43:49,458
One and two are already sick of my face.

590
00:43:49,541 --> 00:43:52,666
You're such a funny man, sir.

591
00:43:52,750 --> 00:43:56,916
By the way, did you get my gift
for your boy's birthday?

592
00:43:57,000 --> 00:44:01,583
Oh my God.
I forgot to thank you directly.

593
00:44:01,666 --> 00:44:04,291
Thank you so much, sir.
You really didn't have to.

594
00:44:05,291 --> 00:44:06,666
Not at all.

595
00:44:06,750 --> 00:44:08,625
You did say he wanted a Wubicon.

596
00:44:08,708 --> 00:44:10,000
Correct, sir.

597
00:44:10,083 --> 00:44:14,625
Kids these days have expensive taste.

598
00:44:14,708 --> 00:44:18,250
That's good, not like back
in our day, struggling.

599
00:44:18,333 --> 00:44:20,125
You're right again, sir.

600
00:44:20,208 --> 00:44:22,625
All right, then, I'm off to watch a movie.

601
00:44:23,166 --> 00:44:25,125
Very well, sir.

602
00:44:25,208 --> 00:44:28,791
If anything comes up,
just text me, all right?

603
00:44:28,875 --> 00:44:29,875
Will do.

604
00:44:29,958 --> 00:44:31,708
I'm here whenever you need me.

605
00:44:31,791 --> 00:44:33,000
Have a great shift.

606
00:44:33,083 --> 00:44:34,250
And you have a good rest, sir.

607
00:44:34,333 --> 00:44:35,875
- Good night, Mr. Sapto.
- Good night, sir.

608
00:44:39,041 --> 00:44:40,750
Find the culprit now!

609
00:44:43,416 --> 00:44:47,125
What do you mean you saw
Tokek walk into his cell?

610
00:44:47,208 --> 00:44:50,083
I swear it was him. He was real.

611
00:44:50,166 --> 00:44:51,458
Not like some see-through ghost.

612
00:44:51,541 --> 00:44:53,291
Like you know
what a ghost even looks like.

613
00:44:53,375 --> 00:44:54,500
That's what they say, right?

614
00:44:54,583 --> 00:44:58,083
Six, if you keep making things up,
we will beat you up ourselves.

615
00:44:58,166 --> 00:44:59,958
Have you ever seen me this serious?

616
00:45:00,041 --> 00:45:01,500
I don't believe you.

617
00:45:02,708 --> 00:45:03,625
Still...

618
00:45:04,916 --> 00:45:06,000
Hey, what are you doing here?!

619
00:45:06,083 --> 00:45:07,625
- Hey, shush!
- What's with you?!

620
00:45:07,708 --> 00:45:09,458
- Stay away.
- What's wrong with you?

621
00:45:09,541 --> 00:45:10,791
He can't! He shouldn't be here!

622
00:45:10,875 --> 00:45:11,625
Stay away!

623
00:45:11,708 --> 00:45:14,000
- Six! Dimas, stay here.
- No, no, no!

624
00:45:14,083 --> 00:45:16,416
- Kindness will do you good.
- You stay there!

625
00:45:16,500 --> 00:45:18,541
Don't stay here! Go!
Please, just listen to me!

626
00:45:18,625 --> 00:45:19,916
If you act like this...

627
00:45:20,708 --> 00:45:22,666
- Sit down!
- No, let him leave so Six calms down.

628
00:45:22,750 --> 00:45:24,583
- Be quiet!
- Calm down.

629
00:45:26,583 --> 00:45:28,625
What are you doing on that side?
Go over there!

630
00:45:31,708 --> 00:45:32,625
Hey.

631
00:45:32,708 --> 00:45:36,958
Do you think they're suspicious of us?

632
00:45:37,041 --> 00:45:39,125
I mean, we always clashed
with Tokek's gang.

633
00:45:39,208 --> 00:45:43,125
But honestly, we'd be better off
if the police investigated.

634
00:45:43,208 --> 00:45:46,416
But that won't happen.
The officers will handle it themselves.

635
00:45:46,875 --> 00:45:48,833
So now we've got two problems.

636
00:45:48,916 --> 00:45:50,625
First, the prison officers,

637
00:45:50,708 --> 00:45:51,666
Second...

638
00:45:53,583 --> 00:45:57,625
Them. They'll think we did it.

639
00:45:58,208 --> 00:46:00,083
Anggoro's gonna protect us, right?

640
00:46:00,166 --> 00:46:01,666
Allah will protect you.

641
00:46:07,000 --> 00:46:08,208
What's wrong with Anton?

642
00:46:08,291 --> 00:46:11,625
His wife ran off with all their savings.

643
00:46:12,916 --> 00:46:14,458
Wait... you see that?

644
00:46:14,541 --> 00:46:16,083
The red thing around Anton?

645
00:46:16,166 --> 00:46:17,625
- What are you talking about?
- That!

646
00:46:17,708 --> 00:46:19,333
Like red smoke!

647
00:46:19,416 --> 00:46:20,916
Stop being creepy, Six!

648
00:46:21,000 --> 00:46:23,041
- What?
- Nothing's there!

649
00:46:23,125 --> 00:46:25,916
- It looks like smoke!
- What do you mean?

650
00:46:26,000 --> 00:46:27,083
Red smoke on his body.

651
00:46:27,166 --> 00:46:32,541
- I'm fine. I said I'm fine!
- Don't make a scene.

652
00:46:33,375 --> 00:46:35,041
- Around him.
- Enough.

653
00:46:35,125 --> 00:46:36,041
Stop it.

654
00:46:36,125 --> 00:46:36,958
Shut up!

655
00:46:42,625 --> 00:46:43,708
Food's ready!

656
00:46:44,541 --> 00:46:49,041
Let's eat.

657
00:46:53,291 --> 00:46:54,916
What's going on? What happened?

658
00:47:01,625 --> 00:47:04,000
You all know the situation.

659
00:47:05,458 --> 00:47:07,125
I won't say much.

660
00:47:07,625 --> 00:47:11,083
Talking's not my job.

661
00:47:11,166 --> 00:47:12,916
Yet you never stop talking.

662
00:47:13,000 --> 00:47:16,083
If anyone knows who committed
this horrific crime,

663
00:47:16,166 --> 00:47:17,458
step forward now.

664
00:47:19,833 --> 00:47:20,750
Come.

665
00:47:21,666 --> 00:47:22,916
Quickly.

666
00:47:23,000 --> 00:47:23,958
Sir.

667
00:47:24,041 --> 00:47:25,375
- Yes?
- I'm scared, sir.

668
00:47:26,083 --> 00:47:30,708
I saw the body. That death wasn't natural.

669
00:47:31,250 --> 00:47:34,375
Why haven't the police come?

670
00:47:46,375 --> 00:47:50,250
I've been trying to keep you all safe.

671
00:47:50,333 --> 00:47:54,166
But I guess you just want to
make things difficult!

672
00:47:56,750 --> 00:47:57,708
Hey.

673
00:47:57,791 --> 00:47:59,750
Did anyone ask you to help him?

674
00:48:03,291 --> 00:48:04,166
No.

675
00:48:04,708 --> 00:48:06,333
Do I need permission for that?

676
00:48:07,041 --> 00:48:08,291
Where were you this morning?

677
00:48:08,375 --> 00:48:11,083
Where else could I go? I'm a prisoner.

678
00:48:15,958 --> 00:48:18,000
You think this is a joke?

679
00:48:19,958 --> 00:48:23,958
Where were you when Tokek was murdered?

680
00:48:24,041 --> 00:48:25,708
In my cell. I have witnesses.

681
00:48:25,791 --> 00:48:27,416
Who? Your friends?

682
00:48:28,750 --> 00:48:30,541
The CCTV might show something else.

683
00:48:30,625 --> 00:48:32,833
What CCTV? They're all dead.

684
00:48:32,916 --> 00:48:33,958
Exactly.

685
00:48:34,833 --> 00:48:38,833
Which means we can do whatever we want.

686
00:48:39,375 --> 00:48:44,250
Nowadays, anything can be staged.

687
00:48:48,125 --> 00:48:50,000
How much longer are you in for?

688
00:48:51,041 --> 00:48:52,000
Seven months?

689
00:48:53,833 --> 00:48:54,916
Forget it.

690
00:48:55,500 --> 00:49:02,541
A murder case like this
could add another 20 years.

691
00:49:11,666 --> 00:49:13,541
There's no breakfast today.

692
00:49:15,416 --> 00:49:18,625
No lunch.

693
00:49:20,000 --> 00:49:21,375
And no dinner.

694
00:49:22,958 --> 00:49:26,125
If no one's coming forward,

695
00:49:27,583 --> 00:49:31,916
there'll be no food
tomorrow or ever again!

696
00:49:32,666 --> 00:49:35,500
To help you understand
what discipline means,

697
00:49:35,958 --> 00:49:41,625
I'm cutting off

698
00:49:41,708 --> 00:49:47,041
electricity, water,

699
00:49:47,125 --> 00:49:51,875
anything that makes your life easier.

700
00:49:52,541 --> 00:49:56,208
You want to act like animals?

701
00:49:56,291 --> 00:50:00,291
Then you'll be treated like animals!

702
00:50:20,000 --> 00:50:21,666
- You piece of shit!
- Stay calm.

703
00:50:21,750 --> 00:50:24,916
- We're all screwed because of you.
- Don't take the bait!

704
00:50:25,000 --> 00:50:26,625
Fuck you!

705
00:51:52,208 --> 00:51:54,000
You stupid bitch!

706
00:51:54,083 --> 00:51:58,833
I'll escape and kill you myself, bitch!

707
00:54:14,500 --> 00:54:16,125
Why did you kill your boss?

708
00:54:16,208 --> 00:54:18,250
It wasn't me! I didn't kill my boss!

709
00:54:18,666 --> 00:54:20,375
No need to lie. You're not in a court.

710
00:54:20,458 --> 00:54:21,333
I swear!

711
00:54:21,416 --> 00:54:22,458
Even if I did kill him,

712
00:54:22,541 --> 00:54:25,375
no way I could've lifted
and hung him on the ceiling fan!

713
00:54:25,458 --> 00:54:26,875
Then why were you still found guilty?

714
00:54:26,958 --> 00:54:28,083
This is Indonesia.

715
00:54:28,166 --> 00:54:29,750
You think we're in Norway or something?

716
00:54:30,375 --> 00:54:31,916
Maybe your spirit guardian did it.

717
00:54:32,000 --> 00:54:34,291
What? There's no such thing!

718
00:54:34,375 --> 00:54:36,083
Six, come here.

719
00:54:36,833 --> 00:54:37,583
No.

720
00:54:37,666 --> 00:54:39,375
Get over here and tell us what you saw.

721
00:54:41,000 --> 00:54:45,041
After Tokek died, I saw a figure
that looked like him enter your cell.

722
00:54:45,458 --> 00:54:49,666
And just now, after Anton died,
I saw him walking toward you.

723
00:54:50,375 --> 00:54:53,666
I wasn't even at the scene,
so clearly I didn't do it!

724
00:54:54,250 --> 00:54:55,541
I've always been wimpy.

725
00:54:55,625 --> 00:54:57,958
When I was a baby,
even my cries sounded wimpy.

726
00:54:58,041 --> 00:55:00,000
How does that even sound like?!

727
00:55:11,041 --> 00:55:13,500
Actually, I saw something else too.

728
00:55:13,583 --> 00:55:14,625
What?

729
00:55:14,708 --> 00:55:18,500
Before they died,
I saw a red aura around their heads.

730
00:55:18,583 --> 00:55:19,666
Aura?!

731
00:55:19,750 --> 00:55:22,458
I swear I'll stomp on your neck.
You're still making shit up?

732
00:55:23,833 --> 00:55:25,500
I swear, I'll swear on Allah!

733
00:55:25,583 --> 00:55:26,833
But you don't believe in Allah.

734
00:55:26,916 --> 00:55:28,500
Then I'll swear on anything!

735
00:55:28,583 --> 00:55:32,875
Ever since that terrible headache,
I've been seeing weird things.

736
00:55:33,416 --> 00:55:36,791
Tokek and Anton both had
blood-red auras before they died.

737
00:55:36,875 --> 00:55:39,958
How convenient that you just happened
to see their auras.

738
00:55:40,041 --> 00:55:42,291
Now I can see everyone's aura in the dark.

739
00:55:43,041 --> 00:55:44,416
Can you see mine?

740
00:55:44,916 --> 00:55:46,666
- Yes.
- What color?

741
00:55:46,750 --> 00:55:47,583
Grey.

742
00:55:48,250 --> 00:55:49,166
What does it mean?

743
00:55:49,875 --> 00:55:50,625
How would I know?

744
00:55:50,708 --> 00:55:54,083
Then what's the point of you
seeing auras, dumbass?!

745
00:55:54,166 --> 00:55:56,125
Gray aura means confusion.

746
00:55:56,625 --> 00:55:58,791
You're religious.
Why do you believe in such nonsense?

747
00:55:58,875 --> 00:56:06,875
In Islam, though it's not called an aura,
there are verses and hadiths.

748
00:56:06,958 --> 00:56:13,125
"Whoever prays often at night,
their face will shine during the day."

749
00:56:13,208 --> 00:56:15,166
Hadith from Ibn Majah.

750
00:56:15,250 --> 00:56:16,541
Yours is light blue.

751
00:56:17,333 --> 00:56:18,708
Honesty and wisdom.

752
00:56:18,791 --> 00:56:22,083
- Go to hell.
- Man, that's totally made up.

753
00:56:22,166 --> 00:56:24,500
- No way I'm lying. My aura is honesty.
- It's only good when it's him.

754
00:56:25,416 --> 00:56:27,041
Yours is indigo, but murky.

755
00:56:27,125 --> 00:56:28,583
What color is indigo?

756
00:56:29,333 --> 00:56:30,625
Between blue and purple.

757
00:56:30,708 --> 00:56:33,750
If it's murky, it means
you're unsure, conflicted.

758
00:56:33,833 --> 00:56:35,541
Yeah, I'm conflicted about
whether to slap your face or not.

759
00:56:36,125 --> 00:56:39,166
Yours is green, but also murky.

760
00:56:40,958 --> 00:56:42,166
Apathy.

761
00:56:43,458 --> 00:56:46,291
Then what does blood-red mean,
like Tokek's and Anton's?

762
00:56:46,375 --> 00:56:49,000
Anger. Negative energy.

763
00:56:49,083 --> 00:56:51,500
My boss was angry too,
that night before he died.

764
00:56:51,583 --> 00:56:55,083
He fought with his wife,
and our paper was going bankrupt.

765
00:56:55,166 --> 00:57:00,875
So someone's killing people
who have the most negative energy.

766
00:57:00,958 --> 00:57:01,833
But who?

767
00:57:01,916 --> 00:57:02,708
Or what?

768
00:57:02,791 --> 00:57:03,625
Something.

769
00:57:04,166 --> 00:57:05,458
Only if Six isn't making this up.

770
00:57:05,541 --> 00:57:08,416
I'm not! You think it's fun
to see such things?

771
00:57:08,500 --> 00:57:10,916
Enough. We're safe,
since our auras aren't red, right?

772
00:57:11,000 --> 00:57:12,541
Even though they're kinda murky.

773
00:57:12,625 --> 00:57:13,833
Not really.

774
00:57:13,916 --> 00:57:16,791
Auras can change with your mood.

775
00:57:16,875 --> 00:57:20,083
What if it turns red and murky?
How do we fix it?

776
00:57:20,166 --> 00:57:22,208
By doing good deeds.

777
00:57:23,125 --> 00:57:26,875
Cleaning with sincerity, praying, or art.

778
00:57:26,958 --> 00:57:31,166
Doing art can calm you down.
It keeps your aura safe.

779
00:57:31,250 --> 00:57:32,000
Like what?

780
00:57:32,583 --> 00:57:34,916
Painting, singing, dancing.

781
00:57:35,000 --> 00:57:36,500
I can't paint or sing.

782
00:57:36,583 --> 00:57:37,416
Then dance.

783
00:57:37,958 --> 00:57:38,750
I can't dance either.

784
00:57:38,833 --> 00:57:40,625
Everybody can dance.

785
00:57:40,708 --> 00:57:44,333
Screw you. You used to be the quiet one.
Now you won't shut up.

786
00:57:44,416 --> 00:57:48,250
- He's right. It's bullshit.
- Stop fooling around.

787
00:57:48,333 --> 00:57:52,041
- Enough.
- Come here and explain it.

788
00:57:52,708 --> 00:57:55,458
How long does it take
to learn to read the Quran?

789
00:57:55,541 --> 00:57:57,458
If you're diligent, 48 hours.

790
00:57:57,541 --> 00:57:59,250
- That's fast!
- Only if you're diligent.

791
00:58:01,333 --> 00:58:02,541
Hey, wait!

792
00:58:02,625 --> 00:58:03,916
Wait a minute.

793
00:58:04,000 --> 00:58:06,166
- What do you want?
- We want to pray!

794
00:58:06,250 --> 00:58:08,416
Find someplace else. It's full here.

795
00:58:09,916 --> 00:58:13,333
That sucks. Muslims never stop others
from practicing their religion.

796
00:58:15,166 --> 00:58:16,375
Let's just recite in our cells.

797
00:58:16,458 --> 00:58:18,208
We can't. Too filthy and impure.

798
00:58:18,291 --> 00:58:19,291
Then what do we do?

799
00:58:19,750 --> 00:58:22,458
That's not it, babe.

800
00:58:22,541 --> 00:58:25,958
Softly, like a wave...

801
00:58:26,041 --> 00:58:29,750
Hi! For those just joining,
welcome to the class!

802
00:58:29,833 --> 00:58:33,041
Please, take any empty spots.

803
00:58:33,125 --> 00:58:36,791
I'm Novilham. Call me Ilham or Novi.

804
00:58:38,958 --> 00:58:41,625
Let's learn some choreography!

805
00:58:41,708 --> 00:58:44,208
Look at me carefully.
I don't want to repeat myself.

806
00:58:44,291 --> 00:58:45,083
Pay attention, okay?

807
00:58:45,166 --> 00:58:47,916
One, right hand up, left hand up.

808
00:58:48,000 --> 00:58:50,666
Crown, then shampoo, and body soap.

809
00:58:50,750 --> 00:58:55,666
Left tit, right tit, go down,
period cramps, and turn!

810
00:58:55,750 --> 00:58:57,041
Period cramps, and turn!

811
00:58:57,125 --> 00:58:59,375
Go big, then close, go big, then close!

812
00:58:59,458 --> 00:59:06,333
One more, then go down, go up,
shampoo, flip it, turn back.

813
00:59:06,416 --> 00:59:09,875
Twerk, twerk, twerk all the way, go up,
and turn around.

814
00:59:12,583 --> 00:59:13,541
Understood?

815
00:59:14,125 --> 00:59:16,083
Now quick, follow me!

816
00:59:16,166 --> 00:59:17,125
Let's do it together!

817
00:59:17,208 --> 00:59:19,916
Right hand up, left hand up,

818
00:59:20,000 --> 00:59:24,708
crown, then shampoo, and soap.

819
00:59:24,791 --> 00:59:30,125
Left tit, right tit, go down,
period cramps, and turn!

820
00:59:30,208 --> 00:59:31,041
Bang!

821
00:59:31,125 --> 00:59:33,250
Period cramps and turn!

822
00:59:33,333 --> 00:59:36,333
Go big, then close, go big, then close!

823
00:59:36,416 --> 00:59:42,958
One more, then go down, go up,
wash your transparent hair, flip it,

824
00:59:43,041 --> 00:59:47,375
turn back, twerk all the way down,
then go up,

825
00:59:47,458 --> 00:59:48,291
and turn around!

826
00:59:49,708 --> 00:59:53,041
You're not synced at all,
moves are different!

827
00:59:53,125 --> 00:59:55,375
Again from the top! Watch me!

828
00:59:55,833 --> 00:59:57,375
Put one hand up.

829
00:59:57,458 --> 00:59:58,291
Up.

830
00:59:58,375 --> 01:00:01,958
- I heard you can see auras.
- Who told you that?

831
01:00:02,041 --> 01:00:04,041
Left tit, right tit.

832
01:00:04,125 --> 01:00:05,208
What's my aura?

833
01:00:05,916 --> 01:00:08,000
- You can only see it in the dark?
- Yeah.

834
01:00:08,083 --> 01:00:08,958
Hold on.

835
01:00:09,666 --> 01:00:11,583
Period cramp and pose.

836
01:00:11,666 --> 01:00:13,083
Well? Am I safe?

837
01:00:13,708 --> 01:00:15,291
Murky green! Safe!

838
01:00:15,375 --> 01:00:17,458
One more time, go big!

839
01:00:18,250 --> 01:00:19,291
Six, am I safe?

840
01:00:19,375 --> 01:00:21,833
Shampoo, flip your hair!

841
01:00:21,916 --> 01:00:23,583
You too.

842
01:00:23,666 --> 01:00:26,416
Twerk all the way down and go back up.

843
01:00:26,500 --> 01:00:28,125
All of you are green, safe!

844
01:00:28,208 --> 01:00:30,875
Hey! What are you doing in the dark?

845
01:00:30,958 --> 01:00:32,291
Join the group!

846
01:00:32,375 --> 01:00:36,333
You guys just don't appreciate my class.

847
01:00:36,416 --> 01:00:37,375
I'm tired!

848
01:00:39,125 --> 01:00:40,416
All of you get out!

849
01:00:40,500 --> 01:00:41,750
What a waste of my energy.

850
01:00:41,833 --> 01:00:42,958
Get out!

851
01:00:43,416 --> 01:00:47,083
I'm exhausted! This is not the day.

852
01:00:47,166 --> 01:00:49,333
Quick, get out!

853
01:01:08,041 --> 01:01:11,541
I'm worried. Novilham seems so upset.

854
01:01:11,625 --> 01:01:14,041
But he keeps dancing.
He should be safe, right?

855
01:01:15,000 --> 01:01:16,291
That's true...

856
01:01:35,833 --> 01:01:38,083
Why's he so down anyway?

857
01:01:38,166 --> 01:01:42,750
His dance studio was demolished
for a political party headquarters.

858
01:01:42,833 --> 01:01:46,500
Too many parties already, aren't there?
Like floating turds.

859
01:01:47,458 --> 01:01:50,875
Have you actually seen floating turds?
I haven't.

860
01:01:51,833 --> 01:01:53,125
Ever gone looking for them?

861
01:01:53,208 --> 01:01:54,125
No.

862
01:01:54,500 --> 01:01:55,791
For political parties?

863
01:01:55,875 --> 01:01:56,708
No.

864
01:01:56,791 --> 01:01:58,500
See? They're the same thing.

865
01:02:09,000 --> 01:02:11,791
Hopefully, his dancing
keeps his aura safe.

866
01:02:20,458 --> 01:02:22,791
What if he dances in anger?

867
01:02:22,875 --> 01:02:25,083
Is that even possible? Dancing angrily?

868
01:02:25,625 --> 01:02:29,291
Of course, it is.
People pray in anger all the time.

869
01:03:37,666 --> 01:03:40,250
Academic advisor...

870
01:03:40,333 --> 01:03:41,916
Where are you guys going?

871
01:03:42,000 --> 01:03:44,166
Trying to dance instead.
The Quran is hard, man.

872
01:03:46,458 --> 01:03:47,958
First time reciting?

873
01:03:48,041 --> 01:03:49,500
Yeah. We're Christians.

874
01:03:49,583 --> 01:03:51,625
Don't go in yet.
The teacher needs time alone.

875
01:03:51,708 --> 01:03:53,166
Don't tell me what to do.

876
01:04:21,625 --> 01:04:22,375
Fuck!

877
01:04:22,458 --> 01:04:24,333
We were only a few meters away!

878
01:04:24,416 --> 01:04:25,708
Fuck!

879
01:04:25,791 --> 01:04:28,500
Now the cops will definitely show up!

880
01:04:28,583 --> 01:04:31,083
Wrong. We'll be cut off from the outside.

881
01:04:31,166 --> 01:04:34,458
They will cover this up
to hide the drug business here.

882
01:04:34,541 --> 01:04:35,750
His aura was brown.

883
01:04:36,833 --> 01:04:37,750
What?

884
01:04:37,833 --> 01:04:41,291
Novi's aura before he died.
Dark brown. Not red.

885
01:04:41,375 --> 01:04:42,791
What does that mean?

886
01:04:42,875 --> 01:04:46,166
People with dark brown auras,
that's below blood red.

887
01:04:46,250 --> 01:04:48,083
It wasn't anger.
More like boiling frustration.

888
01:04:48,166 --> 01:04:51,833
Wait, so the aura doesn't have to be red
for someone to die?

889
01:04:52,750 --> 01:04:53,666
No.

890
01:04:53,750 --> 01:04:55,625
Even if everyone stays positive,

891
01:04:55,708 --> 01:04:57,500
there'll always be
the least positive person.

892
01:04:57,583 --> 01:04:58,708
And that person's gonna die.

893
01:04:58,791 --> 01:04:59,708
Fuck.

894
01:04:59,791 --> 01:05:03,791
In the end, we're all
going to die one by one.

895
01:05:06,958 --> 01:05:09,208
I can see everyone's aura,
except for one person.

896
01:05:09,625 --> 01:05:10,708
Who?

897
01:05:15,708 --> 01:05:17,625
Tell us what you know about all this!

898
01:05:17,708 --> 01:05:18,625
Talk!

899
01:05:18,708 --> 01:05:20,000
I swear I don't know anything!

900
01:05:20,875 --> 01:05:22,625
This started happening
when you came in here!

901
01:05:22,708 --> 01:05:24,750
Your boss died the same way?
Like the inmates here?

902
01:05:24,833 --> 01:05:27,291
Yes, but I don't know why. I swear!

903
01:05:27,375 --> 01:05:29,208
Since when did this all start?

904
01:05:29,291 --> 01:05:30,958
Since the day my boss died.

905
01:05:31,500 --> 01:05:33,041
Where were you before? Visiting a shaman?

906
01:05:33,125 --> 01:05:35,750
No. Just covering a story
about a forest in Borneo.

907
01:05:36,250 --> 01:05:37,125
What case?

908
01:05:37,666 --> 01:05:41,041
Protected forest cleared for
illegal nickel mining.

909
01:05:41,125 --> 01:05:42,791
Government officials were behind it.

910
01:05:42,875 --> 01:05:44,083
And?

911
01:05:44,166 --> 01:05:45,750
But the strange part is,

912
01:05:47,166 --> 01:05:49,291
dozens of workers died suspiciously.

913
01:05:49,375 --> 01:05:50,250
What were the bodies like?

914
01:05:50,333 --> 01:05:51,250
What do you mean?

915
01:05:51,333 --> 01:05:54,000
How did they die? Stabbed? Shot?

916
01:05:54,083 --> 01:05:55,583
Allah, forgive me.

917
01:05:55,666 --> 01:05:56,958
I don't know who killed them,

918
01:05:57,041 --> 01:05:59,458
but the bodies were carved
and hung in trees.

919
01:05:59,541 --> 01:06:00,958
Like an art installation.

920
01:06:01,041 --> 01:06:03,250
Like sculptures in an exhibit.

921
01:06:03,750 --> 01:06:05,750
Except this was made by
a complete lunatic.

922
01:06:07,750 --> 01:06:09,333
Anything else you remember?

923
01:06:10,000 --> 01:06:11,000
About what?

924
01:06:11,083 --> 01:06:14,625
Anything! Anything that can
help us survive!

925
01:06:15,916 --> 01:06:17,958
That's all, there's nothing else.

926
01:06:18,541 --> 01:06:20,041
Think harder, damn it!

927
01:06:20,125 --> 01:06:21,333
I did!

928
01:06:21,833 --> 01:06:23,458
I've been thinking hard!

929
01:06:23,541 --> 01:06:24,416
Every day!

930
01:06:24,500 --> 01:06:26,708
Wondering how I ended up here!

931
01:06:28,625 --> 01:06:30,166
I think so hard every single day.

932
01:06:30,250 --> 01:06:32,708
I don't know about you guys,

933
01:06:32,791 --> 01:06:34,916
but I've never even gotten into
a shouting match,

934
01:06:35,000 --> 01:06:36,625
let alone a physical fight,

935
01:06:36,708 --> 01:06:38,500
let alone killed someone!

936
01:06:39,083 --> 01:06:42,333
My little brothers are
still in junior high.

937
01:06:43,208 --> 01:06:47,458
When they were babies,
our parents drowned in a flood.

938
01:06:48,166 --> 01:06:50,875
I don't know how they're doing now.

939
01:06:53,750 --> 01:06:55,958
I always think hard. I swear.

940
01:07:01,666 --> 01:07:04,000
I also think about my purpose in life.

941
01:07:05,500 --> 01:07:07,333
My dad was a shaman.

942
01:07:08,166 --> 01:07:09,500
He said he could heal people.

943
01:07:10,208 --> 01:07:13,833
I didn't believe him.
I thought he was a fraud.

944
01:07:14,708 --> 01:07:17,583
He said I was special.

945
01:07:18,916 --> 01:07:20,458
That I had a special gift.

946
01:07:23,166 --> 01:07:27,000
Now that I'm seeing things like this,

947
01:07:28,083 --> 01:07:31,833
I'm also thinking hard about
what this gift is for.

948
01:07:39,458 --> 01:07:42,541
We're all born with a purpose.

949
01:07:45,250 --> 01:07:52,791
Everything in nature has a "telos,"
a natural end or goal.

950
01:07:52,875 --> 01:07:54,500
That's from Aristotle.

951
01:07:54,583 --> 01:08:03,000
Every individual has a unique and personal
calling or a mission,

952
01:08:03,083 --> 01:08:06,583
and that's from Søren Kierkegaard.

953
01:08:06,666 --> 01:08:08,250
Suddenly got smart?

954
01:08:08,333 --> 01:08:11,500
It's easier to survive in this country
if people think you're dumb.

955
01:08:11,583 --> 01:08:12,833
Less threatening.

956
01:08:14,333 --> 01:08:17,500
We have to have a purpose in this country.

957
01:08:17,583 --> 01:08:20,500
Otherwise, what's the point of life?

958
01:08:20,583 --> 01:08:27,166
So all of us should survive, go out,
and find our purpose.

959
01:08:27,250 --> 01:08:30,875
For that, we have to work together
and find a solution.

960
01:08:30,958 --> 01:08:31,958
Okay?!

961
01:08:32,041 --> 01:08:33,083
Okay.

962
01:08:33,166 --> 01:08:33,875
Okay.

963
01:08:33,958 --> 01:08:35,208
- Okay!
- Okay.

964
01:08:38,041 --> 01:08:39,625
What an eyesore.

965
01:08:39,708 --> 01:08:40,708
Fuck my goat!

966
01:08:44,750 --> 01:08:47,375
After you got back from Borneo,

967
01:08:47,458 --> 01:08:48,958
did you keep following the case?

968
01:08:49,666 --> 01:08:51,750
Even right before I got here,

969
01:08:51,833 --> 01:08:54,250
I was still in touch with the people.

970
01:08:54,333 --> 01:08:56,208
Anyone else died after that?

971
01:08:57,291 --> 01:08:58,458
No.

972
01:09:00,791 --> 01:09:02,000
What is it, Anggoro?

973
01:09:03,208 --> 01:09:04,125
Anggoro?

974
01:09:04,958 --> 01:09:06,583
Whatever it is...

975
01:09:06,666 --> 01:09:07,708
Stay there!

976
01:09:08,791 --> 01:09:12,791
Whatever killed those people,
it followed Dimas to Jakarta.

977
01:09:12,875 --> 01:09:14,333
It's here with us.

978
01:09:19,083 --> 01:09:21,250
You...

979
01:09:22,208 --> 01:09:23,833
- What are you doing?!
- I'm taking him away.

980
01:09:23,916 --> 01:09:25,125
Hand the kid over!

981
01:09:25,208 --> 01:09:26,291
Why? He didn't kill anyone.

982
01:09:26,375 --> 01:09:29,541
- Since he showed up, people started dying!
- What'll you do with him?

983
01:09:29,625 --> 01:09:30,708
He's not getting out of here alive!

984
01:09:30,791 --> 01:09:32,500
Hand him over!

985
01:09:34,500 --> 01:09:35,458
Close it!

986
01:09:35,541 --> 01:09:36,666
Open it, fucker!

987
01:10:32,416 --> 01:10:34,125
Hey.

988
01:10:36,041 --> 01:10:37,208
Give it to me!

989
01:10:40,333 --> 01:10:41,250
Eat this shit!

990
01:10:47,250 --> 01:10:50,833
Fuck!

991
01:10:50,916 --> 01:10:52,791
Eat this shit!

992
01:11:10,500 --> 01:11:11,541
Anggoro!

993
01:11:11,625 --> 01:11:12,375
What?

994
01:11:12,458 --> 01:11:13,833
- Your aura!
- What about it?

995
01:11:13,916 --> 01:11:15,625
It turned red!

996
01:11:18,458 --> 01:11:20,375
- What do I do?
- Tone it down!

997
01:11:20,458 --> 01:11:22,416
Pray! Or do art!

998
01:11:23,041 --> 01:11:23,750
Right now?

999
01:11:23,833 --> 01:11:26,958
You'll die! Do it now! Pray or do art!

1000
01:11:38,375 --> 01:11:39,166
Fight back, you shithead!

1001
01:11:57,833 --> 01:11:59,000
He's safe.

1002
01:11:59,083 --> 01:12:00,708
You're safe, Anggoro!

1003
01:12:05,166 --> 01:12:06,791
- You like that?
- Fuck you!

1004
01:12:08,875 --> 01:12:10,458
What about Bimo?

1005
01:12:13,291 --> 01:12:15,458
Hey, answer me! Be fair, man!

1006
01:12:20,958 --> 01:12:22,166
Reddish gray.

1007
01:12:23,000 --> 01:12:25,208
Bimo! Your aura is red!

1008
01:12:26,875 --> 01:12:28,333
Your aura is red!

1009
01:12:28,416 --> 01:12:29,458
I'm not dancing! Gross!

1010
01:12:29,541 --> 01:12:31,791
Look, the shadow has appeared.

1011
01:12:31,875 --> 01:12:32,750
Bimo!

1012
01:12:32,833 --> 01:12:33,958
You will die!

1013
01:12:35,791 --> 01:12:38,416
Our Father who art in Heaven,
hallowed be Thy name.

1014
01:12:38,500 --> 01:12:43,083
Thy Kingdom come, Thy will be done
on earth as it is in Heaven.

1015
01:12:43,166 --> 01:12:46,375
Give us this day our daily bread
and forgive us our trespasses as we...

1016
01:12:47,125 --> 01:12:47,916
Bimo!

1017
01:12:49,000 --> 01:12:51,000
He's safe!

1018
01:12:51,083 --> 01:12:52,416
- You're safe!
- I'm safe?

1019
01:12:52,500 --> 01:12:53,708
You're safe, Bimo!

1020
01:13:06,833 --> 01:13:07,791
Hey!

1021
01:13:15,375 --> 01:13:17,416
Listen up, all of you.

1022
01:13:17,500 --> 01:13:21,958
We may be enemies. Rivals.

1023
01:13:22,375 --> 01:13:28,375
But when we're in danger,
we must stand together.

1024
01:13:28,916 --> 01:13:32,041
That's the only way we all survive.

1025
01:13:33,166 --> 01:13:34,208
After he's gone,

1026
01:13:36,458 --> 01:13:39,875
we can go back to hating each other.

1027
01:13:59,583 --> 01:14:00,916
Wait!

1028
01:14:02,541 --> 01:14:06,416
You think the ghost will just disappear
if Dimas dies? No!

1029
01:14:06,500 --> 01:14:11,208
This isn't a regular ghost.
You can't just get rid of it.

1030
01:14:11,291 --> 01:14:14,000
If he dies, it'll just move on
to the next host.

1031
01:14:14,083 --> 01:14:16,125
And we don't know who.

1032
01:14:17,250 --> 01:14:19,666
We can't fight something
we don't understand.

1033
01:14:20,416 --> 01:14:22,625
And Dimas is the key
to understanding this ghost.

1034
01:14:22,708 --> 01:14:24,291
He brought it here

1035
01:14:24,375 --> 01:14:27,666
and will help us figure out
how to stop it.

1036
01:14:27,750 --> 01:14:31,208
If he dies? We have no answers.

1037
01:14:31,958 --> 01:14:34,500
We just wait for our turn to die,
one by one.

1038
01:14:34,583 --> 01:14:35,541
Is that what you want?

1039
01:14:37,208 --> 01:14:38,791
I mean, look at him.

1040
01:14:38,875 --> 01:14:40,083
He's a wimp.

1041
01:14:40,875 --> 01:14:43,083
But look how deadly the ghost is.

1042
01:14:43,166 --> 01:14:45,666
What if it attaches to someone brutal?

1043
01:14:45,750 --> 01:14:47,916
It might kill all of us in one go.

1044
01:14:49,041 --> 01:14:50,125
That's why

1045
01:14:51,125 --> 01:14:53,083
Dimas must not die!

1046
01:14:53,541 --> 01:14:55,291
He's the key!

1047
01:15:04,250 --> 01:15:06,541
I'm the key!

1048
01:15:06,625 --> 01:15:09,041
I shouldn't die!

1049
01:16:02,958 --> 01:16:04,500
I don't understand

1050
01:16:05,791 --> 01:16:13,375
why stupid people make their lives
harder than they need to be.

1051
01:16:14,291 --> 01:16:20,416
Look at the result of teaching you peace.

1052
01:16:20,958 --> 01:16:23,541
Are you all allergic to peace?

1053
01:16:23,625 --> 01:16:25,750
